{"title":"Career roadmap · Polymer Technologist","role":"Polymer Technologist","summary":"A Polymer Technologist applies chemistry, materials science and manufacturing principles to develop, process, test and improve polymers, plastics, elastomers, composites, coatings and adhesives.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Polymer Science / Industrial Chemistry"},"about":[{"label":"Primary stack","text":"Polymer chemistry + processing + characterisation + quality + industrial safety"},{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Strong alignment. Build both laboratory/material-characterisation capability and industrial processing knowledge."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For B.Sc. Polymer Science / Industrial Chemistry, this is a directly aligned career. Graduates can target laboratory, quality, process, production and junior R&D roles. Advanced polymer R&D generally benefits from an M.Sc./M.Tech."}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build polymer chemistry, materials science, processing, testing and industrial-quality skills."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Enter as Polymer Technologist, Polymer QC Analyst, Materials Analyst, Process Technologist or R&D Associate."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress toward Senior Polymer Technologist, Polymer R&D Specialist, Materials Specialist or Process Specialist."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Move toward R&D Lead, Materials Scientist, Technical Manager, Polymer Development Manager or Materials Innovation Lead."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"General, organic and physical chemistry"},{"text":"NPTEL + university labs"},{"text":"Laboratory records"},{"text":"Chemistry foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Polymer chemistry + analytical chemistry"},{"text":"NPTEL + laboratory work"},{"text":"Polymer identification exercise"},{"text":"Polymer fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Polymer structure, properties and additives"},{"text":"Textbooks + labs"},{"text":"Material-property analysis"},{"text":"Materials knowledge"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Polymer processing and testing"},{"text":"Industrial labs + coursework"},{"text":"Processing experiment"},{"text":"Manufacturing"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Rheology, composites, degradation and QC"},{"text":"Research papers + industry projects"},{"text":"Materials-testing report"},{"text":"Industrial readiness"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Industrial/research internship"},{"text":"Polymer manufacturer/R&D lab"},{"text":"Internship project"},{"text":"Employability"}],[{"text":"Final Year / Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Advanced polymer specialisation"},{"text":"Research + industry"},{"text":"Major project"},{"text":"Specialisation"}],[{"text":"Final Year / Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Job/PG preparation"},{"text":"Technical preparation"},{"text":"Portfolio + technical CV"},{"text":"Career readiness"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"h","text":"Chemistry"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Organic Chemistry"},{"text":"Physical Chemistry"},{"text":"Analytical Chemistry"},{"text":"Industrial Chemistry"},{"text":"Chemical Thermodynamics"},{"text":"Reaction Chemistry"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Polymer science"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Polymer Chemistry"},{"text":"Polymerisation Techniques"},{"text":"Polymer Physics"},{"text":"Polymer Characterisation"},{"text":"Polymer Blends"},{"text":"Polymer Composites"},{"text":"Elastomers"},{"text":"Thermoplastics"},{"text":"Thermosetting Polymers"},{"text":"Biopolymers"},{"text":"Functional Polymers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Processin